<title>USA: British Petroleum Co Plc Q3 net up sharply.</title>
<headline>British Petroleum Co Plc Q3 net up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.47		    $0.80</p>
<p> Net		    1,154,000		  278,000</p>
<p> Revs		  17,135,000	     15,280,000</p>
<p>		     Nine Months</p>
<p> Shr			  $6.84		    $4.40</p>
<p> Net		    3,192,000		    2,026</p>
<p> Revs		  48,800,000	     42,497,000</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: U.S. dollar results on a historical cost basis provided by BP.</p>
<p>Net includes inventory holding gain $200 million vs loss $159 million in quarter and gain $378 million vs loss $6 million in 9 months.</p>
<p>Net also includes net exceptional losses of $60 million vs $394 million in quarter and $160 million vs $357 million in 9 months.</p>
<p>This results in replacement cost profit before exceptional items of $1.01 bln, or $2.16/shr, vs $831 million, or $1.80/shr in the quarter and $2.97 bln, or $6.37/shr, vs $2.39 bln, or $5.18/shr, in nine months.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
